{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"injurious-pugnacious-azurevase","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nStep-7 class review under auspicial-friended-merganser (2ec7-be89-9b01-496a) found ADDITIONAL members of the same construct class beyond that ticket's explicitly enumerated 9 sites. These derive a REPO/CONFIG root from the store path via variants the enumerated list and the AC#4 guard (scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py, which matches only the bare 'dirname(tracker)' and 'dirname(tracker_dir())' forms) do NOT cover:\n\n### Config/gate reads (str(tracker) variant) — advisory-only impact, closest siblings\n- src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:274 and :286 — cfg_root=os.path.dirname(str(tracker)) into description_cap_warning() and duplicate_create_warning(); cfg_root feeds compose_config() (verify.max_ticket_description_chars, verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets) AND _plan_review_gate_applies(). On a relocated store these read an empty config, so the save-time description-cap heads-up and duplicate probe are silently suppressed. ADVISORY only (never blocks a write), which is why it is milder than the enumerated AC#1 gate escape. repo_root is in scope in create_core (composer.py:125).\n- src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:141 — same cfg_root=os.path.dirname(str(tracker)) in _edit_description_warning(); needs repo_root threaded from edit_core (composer.py:553, calls at :647).\n\n### Config reads (realpath()/abspath() variant) — NEEDS A DESIGN JUDGMENT per site\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:238 — _sync_disabled(dirname(realpath(tracker))) -> compose_config(root).sync.pull (reads.py:220).\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:249 — tickets_branch(dirname(tracker_abs)) -> tickets.branch config.\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:374 — _load_scratch: repo_root = dirname(abspath(tracker)) -> compose_config(root).scratch.base_dir (reads.py:381).\n\nThe realpath/abspath family is genuinely nuanced: these operate on the STORE's OWN git repo (git -C tracker_abs for sync/branch), so for a relocated store the tracker's parent may LEGITIMATELY be the correct root for sync.pull / tickets.branch (the store is its own repo), whereas scratch.base_dir arguably should follow the CODE repo. Resolving each is AC#3's 'or documents why the tracker's parent is correct for it' clause and requires a per-site design decision — which is why it is split OUT of the enumerated-9 ticket rather than folded into that behavior-preserving change.\n\nOther realpath(tracker)-root sites to TRIAGE for the same question (likely legitimate store-repo roots for git/attribution, but verify): compact_txn.py:523, compact_rebuild.py:138, compact_plan.py:211, fsck.py:252, fsck_tracker_health.py:82/:203/:373, _proc.py:141, _store/sync.py:311/:312.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. composer.py:274/:286 and composer_edit.py:141 resolve cfg_root from the repo root (repo_root in scope / threaded), not os.path.dirname(str(tracker)). RED->GREEN test that the description-cap warning fires on a relocated store with a low verify.max_ticket_description_chars.\n2. Each reads.py sync/branch/scratch site either resolves from the code repo root OR carries a comment justifying the store's parent as correct, with the design decision recorded.\n3. Triage the realpath(tracker) git/attribution family; fix or document each.\n4. Extend scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py to also flag the str()/realpath()/os.path.abspath() wrapped variants once the legitimate store-repo sites carry a '# repo-root-ok:' sanction, so the guard becomes airtight for the whole class.","id":"c0f6-0fc9-fe48-41bc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"dirname/realpath(tracker)-as-config-root at further sites beyond the enumerated 9 (str()/realpath()/abspath() variants)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787939647799071001,"uuid":"012715b8-c2d0-4fc4-b42f-cc19c914b441"}